      "description": "Why Valvoline Global Operations? At Valvoline Global Operations , we’re proud to be The Original Motor Oil , but we’ve never rested on being first. Founded in 1866, we introduced the world’s first branded motor oil, staking our claim as a pioneer in the automotive and industrial ...",
      "raw_description": "Why Valvoline Global Operations? At Valvoline Global Operations , we’re proud to be The Original Motor Oil , but we’ve never rested on being first. Founded in 1866, we introduced the world’s first branded motor oil, staking our claim as a pioneer in the automotive and industrial solutions industry. Today, as an affiliate of Aramco , one of the world’s largest integrated energy and chemicals companies, we are driven by innovation and committed to creating sustainable solutions for a better future. With a global presence, we develop future-ready products and provide best-in-class services for our partners around the world. For us, originality isn’t just about where we began; it’s about where we’re headed and how we’ll lead the way. We are originality in motion. Our Corporate Values—Care, Integrity, Passion, Unity, And Excellence—are At The Heart Of Everything We Do. These Values Define How We Operate, How We Treat One Another, And How We Engage With Our Partners, Customers, And The Communities We Serve. At Valvoline Global, We Are United In Our Commitment To Treating everyone with care. Acting with unwavering integrity. Striving for excellence in all endeavors. Delivering on our commitments with passion. Collaborating as one unified team. When you join Valvoline Global , you’ll become part of a culture that celebrates creativity, innovation, and excellence. Together, we’re shaping the future of automotive and industrial solutions. Job Purpose Support the Product Marketing function in developing a comprehensive product roadmap for passenger car lubricants for Southeast Asian markets. The role involves industry research, competitive benchmarking, portfolio gap assessment and identification of product opportunities to strengthen Valvoline’s market competitiveness and drive incremental business growth. How You Make An Impact (Job Accountabilities) Conduct industry and market analysis of passenger car lubricants for southeast Asian markets to understand market dynamics, trends and growth opportunities. Undertake competitive benchmarking of key lubricant brands and their product portfolios against Valvoline across viscosity grades, pack sizes, product claims and technical specifications Evaluate Valvoline’s existing product portfolio against market requirements and competitive offerings to identify portfolio gaps and opportunities. Analyze competitive positioning and identify potential product additions, modifications and portfolio optimization opportunities. Conduct competitive analysis on product communications and taglines across online and offline channels. Develop recommendations for a future product portfolio roadmap based on market insights and competitive analysis. Assess potential volume upside and business opportunities arising from identified portfolio gaps and product recommendations Consolidate findings and present actionable recommendations to the Product Marketing Team What You Bring to the Role (Job Qualifications / Education / Skills / Requirements / Capabilities) Currently pursuing a graduate or postgraduate degree in Economics, Business Analytics, Marketing or related disciplines. Strong analytical, research and problem-solving skills. High proficiency in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint Ability to interpret market data, conduct competitive research and translate findings into actionable business insights Strong written and verbal English communication skills. Basic understanding of business, marketing and commercial concepts Prior exposure to market research, data analysis or business projects would be an advantage. Competencies Desired Research and Data Interpretation Analytical thinking and problem solving Business understanding Initiative and ownership Learning agility Working Conditions / Physical Requirements / Travel Requirements Working Conditions / Physical Requirements: Primarily office based -role involving market research, data analysis, desk-based assignments and presentations Travel Requirements: No travel required Valvoline Global is an equal opportunity employer . We are dedicated to fostering an environment where every individual feels valued, respected, and empowered to contribute their unique perspectives and skills. We strictly prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind, regardless of race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability, genetics, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to ensuring accessibility throughout our recruitment process. If you require a reasonable accommodation to participate in any stage of the recruitment or selection process, please contact us at:. Email: Valvolineglobalcareers@valvolineglobal.com This contact information is solely for accommodation requests. For inquiries about application status, please use the appropriate channels listed in your application materials. Are You Ready to Make an Impact? At Valvoline Global, we’re looking for passionate and talented individuals to join our journey of innovation and excellence. Are you ready to shape the future with us? Apply today. Requisition ID: 2793",
