      "description": "Role: Product Intern Fluento Locations: Bengaluru, Karnataka, India About LEAD Group: LEAD Group is India's largest and fastest-growing School EdTech company, on a mission to provide excellent education to every child. Since 2012, LEAD has transformed learning outcomes through te...",
      "raw_description": "Role: Product Intern Fluento Locations: Bengaluru, Karnataka, India About LEAD Group: LEAD Group is India's largest and fastest-growing School EdTech company, on a mission to provide excellent education to every child. Since 2012, LEAD has transformed learning outcomes through technology-driven solutions that empower schools, teachers, and students. Today, LEAD partners with 8,000+ schools, serves 3.5 million+ students, supports 50,000+ teachers, and operates across 400+ cities and towns in India. Through its Integrated School EdTech System and flagship programs, including LEAD, PINNACLE+, PROPEL, and PINNACLE, LEAD enables schools of every type to deliver measurable learning outcomes at scale. By 2028, LEAD aims to impact 25 million students, making quality education accessible to children across India. About Fluento: Fluento is India's first AI-powered Spoken English program, designed to help every student become a confident English speaker. At the heart of Fluento is Ms. Curie , an AI tutor who provides personalized 1:1 speaking practice, instant feedback, and adaptive learning experiences. By combining cutting-edge AI with strong pedagogy, Fluento makes high-quality spoken English coaching accessible to every child. Role Overview: We're looking for a Product Intern to help build India's first AI tutor. This is a highly hands-on role where you'll work directly with state-of-the-art AI models, experiment rapidly, and turn ideas into real learning activities used by students. You'll collaborate closely with product, content, design, and engineering teams to create experiences that are both educational and delightful. What You'll Do Build AI-powered experiences: Experiment with LLMs and design prompts that power conversations, activities, and personalized learning experiences. Design learning activities: Convert English-learning concepts into engaging, interactive speaking activities suited to different age groups and proficiency levels. Experiment and iterate: Test AI outputs, identify gaps, refine prompts, and continuously improve the quality of AI interactions. Evaluate AI behaviour: Assess whether the AI tutor's responses are accurate, age-appropriate, engaging, and aligned with the intended learning objectives. Think like a product owner: Identify opportunities to improve the student experience, break down problems, and take ideas from concept to execution. Collaborate cross-functionally: Work with product, content, design, and engineering teams to build and launch learning experiences. What We're Looking For Problem Solving & Product Thinking Curious, analytical, and excited to explore new ideas. Able to break down ambiguous problems and find practical solutions. Strong attention to detail and a bias toward experimentation and iteration. Comfortable balancing creativity with structured thinking. Comfortable taking ownership of tasks, moving quickly, and learning through experimentation. AI & Prompt Engineering Hands-on experience working with leading AI models such as GPT, Claude, and Gemini. Ability to systematically iterate on prompts to achieve consistent, high-quality outputs. Strong prompt-writing skills, with a focus on simplicity, efficiency, and reliability. Bonus: You've built something with AI—whether it's a side project, prototype, workflow, agent, or experiment. Be sure to share links, demos, or examples in your application. Technical Curiosity Basic understanding of how modern AI systems and LLMs work, including their strengths and limitations. (Good to have) Interest in how AI products are designed, built, and improved. Eagerness to learn new tools and technologies quickly. Collaboration & Communication Clear communicator who can explain ideas, feedback, and decisions effectively. Comfortable working cross-functionally with product, content, design, and engineering teams. Open to feedback and able to iterate quickly in a fast-paced environment.",
