      "description": "Aleph Technologies is hiring SDE Interns (Full Stack & AI). Location: Pune (Hybrid). Remote within India also considered. Duration: 6 months, starting December (slightly flexible) Type: Paid internship BEFORE YOU APPLY Your resume MUST include: • A link to your GitHub • At least ...",
      "raw_description": "Aleph Technologies is hiring SDE Interns (Full Stack & AI). Location: Pune (Hybrid). Remote within India also considered. Duration: 6 months, starting December (slightly flexible) Type: Paid internship BEFORE YOU APPLY Your resume MUST include: • A link to your GitHub • At least one project you built, with a link (repo, deployed app or demo video). For group projects, say clearly which parts were yours. We look at what you've built before anything else. Applications without GitHub and project links will not be reviewed. ABOUT ALEPH Aleph Technologies builds intelligent systems that solve complex operational challenges in asset-intensive industries, including aviation and logistics. Our product, Aleph Aero, is an AI-powered airport operations platform. It helps large hub airports plan how they run, respond to disruptions in real time, and replace Excel spreadsheets and clunky legacy systems with something planners want to use. We are a small, fast-moving team. Interns work directly with the founding team on production systems, not side projects. THE ROLE Most of the work is on the backend. You'll work on a Python codebase that covers API services, optimisation, simulation, analytics and an AI agent layer, and on the screens airport planners use. This is not a \"fetch coffee and watch\" internship. You will write code that ships, take part in design discussions, and see your work used in real operational settings. WHAT YOU'LL DO • Build and extend backend services and APIs in Python, guided by senior engineers • Build features in our AI agent layer: LLM tool-calling that reads from and acts on the operational model • Test and evaluate AI behaviour on real scenarios, and find out where it breaks • Turn real operational data (CSV, Excel, JSON) into models that help planners make decisions • Work out what the data can and can't tell us, and write down your assumptions and limits • Build and refine React screens that show your work to planners • Write tests, debug issues, and improve your work based on feedback • Work in short build–deploy–learn cycles through Git, pull requests and async communication MUST HAVES • Solid Python fundamentals • Some backend experience from internships, coursework or personal projects (APIs, data models, services) • Comfort with Git and collaborative workflows • You can debug, not just copy and paste, and you can explain your own code • Comfort working with data in tables, spreadsheets and files • Good written communication (we're async-first and distributed) • Self-starter energy: you don't wait to be told what to do next GREAT TO HAVES • FastAPI, Flask or a similar framework • Any of: SQLAlchemy, Postgres, NetworkX, pytest, async Python • Hands-on work with LLM APIs, function/tool calling or agent frameworks (e.g. LangGraph) • Basic React and TypeScript • Interest in simulation, optimisation, queueing or operations research • Interest in aviation, logistics or operations • Anything you've built end to end and can show We care about what you can build and how you think, not where you went to school. Pre-final and final year students and recent graduates are all welcome. WHY ALEPH • Real impact from day one: your work is used by airport planners at large international hub airports • Direct access to the founding team, with no layers of middle management • Ownership of real work in the product, not a corner of someone else's • Regular mentorship and real feedback • Hard, meaningful problems: modelling, optimisation, AI agents and real operational data • A clear path to full-time: strong performers may convert based on performance, impact and business needs HOW TO APPLY Apply through LinkedIn and answer all the screening questions. We review applications on a rolling basis. Shortlisted candidates will get an email with the next steps. Aleph Technologies is an equal opportunity employer. We value diverse perspectives and believe the best teams are built from people with different backgrounds and experiences.",
