      "description": "Line of Service Advisory Industry/Sector Not Applicable Specialism Data, Analytics & AI Management Level Associate Job Description & Summary A career within Data and Analytics services will provide you with the opportunity to help organisations uncover enterprise insights and dri...",
      "raw_description": "Line of Service Advisory Industry/Sector Not Applicable Specialism Data, Analytics & AI Management Level Associate Job Description & Summary A career within Data and Analytics services will provide you with the opportunity to help organisations uncover enterprise insights and drive business results using smarter data analytics. We focus on a collection of organisational technology capabilities, including business intelligence, data management, and data assurance that help our clients drive innovation, growth, and change within their organisations in order to keep up with the changing nature of customers and technology. We make impactful decisions by mixing mind and machine to leverage data, understand and navigate risk, and help our clients gain a competitive edge. Creating business intelligence from data requires an understanding of the business, the data, and the technology used to store and analyse that data. Using our Rapid Business Intelligence Solutions, data visualisation and integrated reporting dashboards, we can deliver agile, highly interactive reporting and analytics that help our clients to more effectively run their business and understand what business questions can be answered and how to unlock the answers. Hiring Chartered Accountants Faster, better, and stronger finance functions significantly contribute to organization- wide agility, results and effectiveness. Finance has been in the midst of a digital revolution coupled with new-age operating models and capabilities. These value levers have increasingly led to bigger and more sustained outcomes from Finance Transformation. We believe these are irreversible trends in the medium term and finance teams must take advantage of this opportune time to transform. We work closely with finance leaders and draw on industry trends, insights, accelerators, and our body of work to reimagine their people, processes and technology with a clear roadmap of how value can be realised. We look well beyond the obvious and partner with clients to frame the potential value, levers and then help implement the roadmap in a credible way that builds confidence and buy-in from all stakeholders. We work in small cross- functional and efficient teams and run iterative sprints to enable incremental and rapid change delivering fast results. Managing business performance in today’s complex and rapidly changing business environment is crucial for any organization’s short-term and long-term success. But ensuring compliance with the continual changes to regulatory requirements, and the ability to plan and monitor performance against plans and budgets, is quite challenging. As part of the Technology Consulting –Data & Analytics Practice, we leverage opportunities around digital disruption to deliver technology enabled transformation to our clients . Within the Technology Consulting practice, our FS D&A competency - Risk, Reg & Finance Data team works on transformational engagements from strategy through execution, helping our clients solve business problems using Data & Analytics technology as an enabler. Some of our key focus areas include:  Ind AS 109 / IFRS9 implementation covering ECL, EIR  Profitability analysis and Cost Management covering areas such as Activity based Costing, Segmental reporting, Dupont analysis, CFO digital playbook  ALM & FTP engine  Regulatory and Risk Reporting Implementation & Risk analytics  Regulatory & Risk Change Management (IRAC, BCBS, Exposure, NSFR, LCR, RWA, Risk based supervision)  Global Markets Change Management  Reconciliation Management & Automation  Pricing Analytics Roles and responsibilities The Consultant will be working for the Technology Consulting - FS D&A competency - Risk, Reg & Finance Data team of PwC India in a Business Analyst (BA) role. As a BA with PwC India, you will play a key client-facing role in the engagement execution by working closely with client teams for defining business requirements, understanding regulatory & financial needs & helping the technology teams during solution implementation. You will be provided with varied responsibilities including client acquisition support, assisting in solution design, contributing to engagement execution as a team member and on-ground client management. We also provide our BAs with opportunities to contribute to various thought leadership initiatives. Our BAs are excellent generalists and have a strong ability to work with managers with diverse backgrounds. Essential Skills:  Understands Finance processes. Knowledge of other business functions will be an added advantage  Basic problem solving skills with an ability to use data to draw business insights  Excellent communication skills including proficiency in English language  Proficiency in excel and power point  Self-disciplined and self -motivated  Strong team building, partnership and collaboration skills  Ability to innovate, create lasting relationships and work independently with little supervision The role can be based out of any location where PwC India has its offices with preferred location being Mumbai but will demand traveling to other client locations as well. · · The role can be based out of any location where PwC India has its offices but will demand traveling to other client locations as well as this is a client facing role. Mandatory Skills: CA Fresher Preferred Skills: CA Fresher Years of Experience: 0 Qualification: CA Education (if blank, degree and/or field of study not specified) Degrees/Field of Study required: Degrees/Field of Study preferred: Certifications (if blank, certifications not specified) Required Skills Optional Skills Desired Languages (If blank, desired languages not specified) Travel Requirements Available for Work Visa Sponsorship? Government Clearance Required? Job Posting End Date",
