      "description": "Discover your future at Citi Working at Citi is far more than just a job. A career with us means joining a team of more than 230,000 dedicated people from around the globe. At Citi, you’ll have the opportunity to grow your career, give back to your community and make a real impac...",
      "raw_description": "Discover your future at Citi Working at Citi is far more than just a job. A career with us means joining a team of more than 230,000 dedicated people from around the globe. At Citi, you’ll have the opportunity to grow your career, give back to your community and make a real impact. Job Overview You're the brains behind our work. You're ready to bring your knowledge from the classroom to the boardroom, and Citi wants to help you get there. Whether it's honing your skills or building your network, we know that success can't come without growth. Our programs equip you with the knowledge and training you need to play a valuable role in your team and establish a long-term career here. At Citi, we value internal mobility, and career growth is not a question of if, but when. Citi is looking for Apprentices to join our various divisions. Here at Citi, the Apprenticeship Program is intended to help you build a broad skill set and accelerate your career growth by gaining exposure to numerous day-to-day activities. Your time here will look something like this... The Apprenticeship Program begins in December/January with a short induction, providing apprentices with an overview of Citi, a technology training session, and an introduction to Citi's divisions. As an apprentice you will gain hands on work experience with deliverables and will be expected to add value to their teams during the 12 months. In addition to your daily work, Apprentices can expand their networks here at Citi. We provide you with the knowledge and skills you need to succeed . The Apprenticeship Program is a 12-months opportunity in India. The Program will provide Apprentices with on-the-job-training supporting one of Citi's Business Groups. Opportunities are offered in Banking, Markets, Services, Wealth, Operations, Technology, Internal Audit, HR, Services, Risk and Control) Who we think will be a great fit.. . We're looking for motivated individuals who are naturally curious and eager to start their careers in financial services. If you have a knack for problem solving, and you enjoy brainstorming creative ideas, Citi is the right place for you! We value diversity and so do you. We'll also be looking for the following: Enthusiasm to learn about the wide range of roles within assigned business/function Ability to work independently and in a team environment with strong communication skills (both written and verbal) at all organizational levels Possesses resiliency to work in a challenging and changing, high volume environment Ability to think globally, creatively, and innovatively Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Advanced MS Word, Access, Excel, and PowerPoint skills We want to hear from you if... You are pursuing a bachelor’s or master’s degree in any discipline with a graduation date between December 2022 and June 2026 Less than 12 months of prior work experience No ESIC/EFP account Ability to relocate domestically Note: Candidates shortlisted will have to register themselves as an apprentice via the government apprentice portal Apprentice – Role & Responsibilities Business Analytics & Information Management Analyst – C00 About AIM: Analytics and Information Management (AIM) is a global community that is driving data-driven transformation across Citi in multiple functions with the objective of creating actionable intelligence for our business leaders. We are a fast-growing organization working with Citi businesses and functions across the world. Excited to grow your career? We value our talented employees, and whenever possible strive to help one of our associates grow professionally before recruiting new talent to our open positions. If you think the open position, you see is right for you, we encourage you to apply! Our people make all the difference in our success. -------------------------------------------------------------- Role is to solve real business problems through strategic decisioning, analytical problem solving and visualization and dashboarding Responsibilities: Technical Expertise - Expertise in data visualization, cleaning, dashboarding & process automation Analyzes external and internal customer data using Hive, Python, Excel etc. to identify areas of opportunity across bank customer lifecycle. Analytic Project Execution – Own and deliver multiple and complex analytic projects. This would require an understanding of business context, conversion of business problems and implementing such solutions to create economic value. Domain expert – Individuals are expected to be domain expert in their sub field, as well as have a holistic view of other business lines to create better solutions. Key fields of focus are new customer acquisition, existing customer management, customer retention, campaign effectiveness, product development, pricing and payment optimization and digital journey. Communication skills – Ability to translate and articulate technical thoughts and ideas to a larger audience including influencing skills with peers and senior management Good process/project management skills Contribute to organizational initiatives in wide range areas including competency development, training, organizational building activities etc. Qualifications: Master’s degree in information technology / information systems / computer applications / Data Science / Business Analytics / MCA in Information Technology / Information Systems / Computer Applications. Good communication skills (both verbal and written) and ability to work with cross-functional partners and team members Adept at managing and manipulating data using Python, Hive/SQL. Prior experience in Data Analytics /Statistical Analysis is a plus Expertise Required: Analytical Skills Data analysis & Data Quality Proficient in formulating analytical methodology, identifying inconsistencies, anomalies & patterns with data Generate actionable Business Insights Coming up with automated Techniques to remove redundancies Good understanding of ML techniques Industry know how on latest & best analytical techniques (Preferred) Tools and Platforms Proficiency in Python, SAS, SQL, Teradata Proficient in MS Excel, PowerPoint and VBA Preferred SAS on Mainframe Big Data/Hadoop environment and coding in Python. Development of Tableau Dashboard Domain Skills: Good understanding of Banking domain (Cards, Deposit, Loans, Wealth management, & Insurance etc.) Audit Framework Data quality framework (Preferred) - Knowledge of Finance Regulations, Understanding of Audit Process ------------------------------------------------------ Job Family Group: Business Strategy, Management & Administration ------------------------------------------------------ Job Family: Administrative Support ------------------------------------------------------ Time Type: Full time ------------------------------------------------------ Most Relevant Skills Please see the requirements listed above. ------------------------------------------------------ Other Relevant Skills For complementary skills, please see above and/or contact the recruiter. ------------------------------------------------------ Citi is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified candidates will receive consideration without regard to their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other characteristic protected by law. If you are a person with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation to use our search tools and/or apply for a career opportunity review Accessibility at Citi. View Citi’s EEO Policy Statement and the Know Your Rights poster.",
